Self-hosted CI admission now requires explicit headroom policy, estimates incoming
peaks from completed local RSS history, and reserves outstanding growth of admitted
jobs alongside the existing declared-memory budget. Unknown probes refuse admission.
This replaces percentage-floor inputs and requires a coordinated runner rollout.
Admission sidecars keep pid as the flock holder and add owner_pid for the owning
worker. RSS accounting uses a live owner_pid even after the keeper is orphaned;
missing or dead owners reserve the full expected peak.
Reserve metadata is read without acquiring its lock; transient missing-holder
metadata retries at the slot interval. Growth uses the same expected peak
checked at admission, independently of the registered budget declaration.
